# Keep the build context tiny + reproducible (the Dockerfile builds from source).
# `**/target`, not `target`: a bare pattern matches only a ROOT path element, so it would
# miss `ee/target`. ee/Dockerfile builds with the MODULE root as context (the ee workspace
# path-deps on `..`), and a developer with a populated ee/target would otherwise ship tens
# of gigabytes of build output into the daemon as context.
**/target
.git
evald-data
node_modules
*.tar.gz
*.zip
# Never let secrets/local state into the builder layer (also forbidden_paths in .ossync.yaml).
.env
secrets
local
